WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.150
- [Narrator] Delivering
millions of COVID-19 vaccines

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.030
involves distribution centers,

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.250
refrigerated trucks and
cold storage facilities.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.520
And each of these could
be a target for hackers.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.910
- COVID has been just a golden opportunity

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.930
for cyber criminals and they've
taken full advantage of it.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.350
- [Narrator] Since the
start of the pandemic,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.300
there have been attempts
to scam individuals

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.770
and businesses for money,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.070
as well as steal vaccine research

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.670
or hold data ransom for a payment.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.880
And a week before the first
vaccinations in the world

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.400
began in the UK, INTERPOL warned
that criminal organizations

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.360
were planning to infiltrate and disrupt

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.200
the vaccine supply chain.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.530
Hackers are looking for a way

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.430
to tamper with the distribution.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.750
The cold chain network
that enables the delivery

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.690
of temperature sensitive
COVID-19 vaccines,

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.350
like the one developed
by Pfizer and BioNTech,

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.610
that has to be kept at
-70 degrees Celsius.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.600
- The payoffs are really big.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.800
The people that are doing it
are increasingly sophisticated.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.670
- [Narrator] So are hackers
targeting the vaccine rollout

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.270
and is there a way to stop them?

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.820
Hackers have been honing
their skills for years

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.620
by going after hospitals.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.310
- The average hospital doesn't
have very good cybersecurity.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.510
Criminals are eager to take advantage

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:21.050
of the concern that the virus has raised.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:23.160
- [Narrator] Jim Lewis
leads a cybersecurity team

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.100
into a Washington based think tank.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.320
He says the easiest tool
for hackers is phishing.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.040
- You send an email out
to a hundred people,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.550
the odds are very good that
two of them will click on it.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.290
What the COVID vaccine creates

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:42.400
is the opportunity to do
this on a massive scale

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.930
and that means you can
ask for a massive ransom.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.630
- [Narrator] If someone
clicks on a malicious link

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.250
or opens an attachment,

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.060
the person may be prompted
to download malware

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.000
or enter login details,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.920
giving the attacker access
to the network and its data.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.040
During the pandemic, phishers setup bait

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.340
with emails sent to hospitals
about COVID-19 prevention

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.610
and setting up pandemic funds.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.500
And now that the vaccines
are on their way,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.550
hackers are taking on new identities

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.770
to infiltrate cold chain companies,

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.770
like ones that manufacture solar panels

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.120
to power refrigerators or IT firms

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.963
that support biotech and
pharmaceutical clients.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.510
- I think the messages were
very specifically crafted

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.860
to get people at these
companies to respond

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:32.070
but in general, this whole
problem of Corona virus

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.820
being a lure for scammers is huge.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.110
- [Narrator] IBM recently tracked down

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.660
a phishing campaign that targeted

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.660
a variety of these companies.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.150
The hacker was disguised
as a project manager

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.640
from the Chinese company, Haier Biomedical

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.990
which, his website says,

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.020
is the world's only complete
cold chain provider.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.610
The writer said it would send an

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:55.180
advance payment of around $220,000.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.070
The message went on to ask that the reader

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.410
review the attached draft contract,

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.440
which is actually a malicious attachment.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.620
IBM says it's unclear if any victims

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.840
clicked on the file and fell for this scam

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:10.210
and doesn't know which nation
state might be behind it.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.520
If there were any victims,

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.360
IBM says the harvested credentials

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.570
could give the hacker insight
into internal communications

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:17.930
as well as methods and plans

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.750
to distribute the COVID-19 vaccine.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.290
Haier Biomedical says it
condemns the perpetrators

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.410
of the phishing email

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.660
and is working with
international organizations

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.010
to ensure that these incidents

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.930
don't deter the fight
against the pandemic.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.650
But if hackers do successfully
access the system,

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.860
they can encrypt the data,
making it unreadable.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.750
This can happen to logistics companies

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.430
responsible for delivering the vaccine.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.260
- And so you could imagine a
locking up the supply chain,

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:48.660
locking up distribution
codes, or locking the trucks

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.700
and saying, unless you pay,
you won't be able to deliver.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.250
- [Narrator] But some
systems in the cold chain

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.030
would be harder to hack.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.400
- Yeah, the actual
operation of a refrigerator,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.360
that would be a specialized
operating system

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.120
and that would be configured
in a way that was unusual so

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.220
they have to figure out how they work.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.960
- [Narrator] So what's
more likely to happen

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.040
is that hackers will go
after low hanging fruit.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.460
- They're already making tons of money

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.930
just hitting standard
windows operating machines.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.250
So if you were working for
a refrigeration company,

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.910
I'd be worried about the sort
of the back office equipment

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:29.910
that the salespeople use,
the laptops and the desktops

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.620
and maybe some of the servers.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.360
- [Narrator] After all,
according to a survey

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.200
by a healthcare IT consultant,

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.930
80% of health professionals
say their hospitals

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.960
still use legacy systems,
such as Windows 2008.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.120
- You need to do basic cyber hygiene

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.970
which includes training,
two factor authentication,

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.720
making sure your patches
and updates are installed,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.530
but on top of that, you
need to back up your data

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.010
and think about how you're
gonna use cloud services.

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:58.100
- [Narrator] But given the high stakes

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.280
of getting more people vaccinated,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.810
no amount of drills may
prepare the cold chain

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:04.210
for the months to come.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:09.210
- This has changed from
efforts to steal the formula,

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.940
to efforts to blackmail
people about distribution.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:15.370
So we're seeing the cyber crime evolve

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.893
when it comes to COVID.

